# Custom applications

Start with a standalone app. Switch to authored `main.roc` when you need
custom routing, extra platform effects, or a shape the generator does not
cover. Reuse `.rocci` components either way.

The default custom app is [Notes](/examples/notes/) (`main.roc` plus
Rocci templates). The [Datastar gallery](/examples/datastar/) is the
pattern gallery. [Snake](/examples/snake/) is an advanced multiplayer
stress demo. [Rocci Blocks](/examples/blocks/) stays standalone; it is
not a `main.roc` app.

## Run Notes

```sh
rocci run examples/rocci/custom/notes --no-window
```

Open `/`. You should see the notes UI. A directory that contains
`main.roc` is a custom app: `rocci run` compiles sibling `.rocci` modules
and starts the authored Roc program. Datastar and snake pin
`crates/rocci-platform` (`import pf.Html` / `import pf.Datastar`).
Sibling `.rocci` modules are not the generated standalone dispatcher;
`main.roc` owns HTTP. A directory without `main.roc` is a
[standalone app](/docs/applications/standalone/).

## Pattern gallery

The [Datastar gallery](/examples/datastar/) ports official Datastar
interaction patterns with authored `main.roc`:

| Route | What to notice |
| --- | --- |
| `/search` | `@let`, `@if`, `@for` |
| `/edit` | `@match` for editing |
| `/todos` | filters and lists |
| `/tabs` | lazy tabs |
| `/validate` | inline validation |

## Advanced demo

[Snake](/examples/snake/) is a Datastar + Rocci multiplayer stress demo:
a hand-written SSE unfold that morphs a full board at about 8 Hz so you
can watch live stream bandwidth. Do not copy that unfold into ordinary
apps; generated `@get:live` already emits the poll loop. Use it when you
need a custom runtime the generator does not cover, or when you want to
measure morph cost.

